/*
 * Declares the GlobalVarRefValue class.
 *
 * GlobalVarRefValue represents a reference to a global variable declared at
 * module scope. Unlike VarRefValue, which refers to variables introduced inside
 * a function body, GlobalVarRefValue refers to variables defined in the module
 * environment and validated by the global generator.
 *
 * A GlobalVarRefValue is always an lvalue and its type is the type of the
 * referenced global variable.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::variable::global
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/variable/global.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-02-27
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
